From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:11:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cullable: Don't cull with actors that have a clip

A shell can clip a window actor while the window reaches past the clip,
for example to keep it on one monitor. Culling still took the window's
opaque region as covering the part the clip hides, so windows and the
background below that area weren't painted and it showed stale
content.

Leave actors with a clip out of culling, as is already done for actors
with active effects: they are painted in full and hide nothing below
them.
---
 src/compositor/meta-cullable.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c b/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c
index 6e55809ec..ad6e22d4a 100644
--- a/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c
+++ b/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c
@@ -118,6 +118,11 @@ cull_out_children_common (MetaCullable    *cullable,
       if (needs_culling && has_active_effects (child))
         needs_culling = FALSE;
 
+      /* A clip hides parts of the actor that its opaque region still
+       * claims to cover, so it can't tell what it obscures either. */
+      if (needs_culling && clutter_actor_has_clip (child))
+        needs_culling = FALSE;
+
       if (needs_culling)
         {
           g_autoptr (MtkRegion) actor_region = NULL;
